Let N be the set of all positive integers. A composition of n ∈ N is an ordered collection of one or
                                      4. Carlitz Compositions

A Carlitz composition of n, introduced in [1], is a composition of n in which no adjacent parts are the
same. We denote the number of Carlitz compositions of n with parts in A (respectively with j parts
in A) by EA (n) (respectively EA (j; n)). The corresponding generating functions are given by
                               X                                  X
                     EA (x) =     EA (n)xn and EA (j; x) =             EA (j; n)xn ,
                               n≥0                                 n≥0

where we define EA (0) = EA (0; 0) = 1 and EA (j; 0) = 0 for j ≥ 1. In particular, EA (0; x) = 1.
