of n − a, except for those compositions of n − a that end in a. Let EA (j, a; n) denote the number
of Carlitz compositions of n that end in a, and let EA (j, a; x) denote the corresponding generating
function, where EA (1, a; n) = 1 if n = a and 0 otherwise. This implies that EA (1, a; x) = xa . The
recursive creation leads to
